From ddea3457be7622fb1339663b43210f11db2b2205 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AKADATA LIMITED <linux@saphira.vm2.uk>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:25:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ccram: residency encoding, fault-in and lifecycle hooks
 (Phase 2B/1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Part of CCRAM — AKADATA LIMITED adaptation of Meta CRAM (see
CRAM.PROVENANCE in linux-saphira-meta-cram; Saphira-original code,
GPL-2.0-only).

Non-present encoding on the purpose-built PTE-marker extension point
(BIT(3) + A/D bits + u32 id, no stolen namespace): fault branch in
handle_pte_marker discharging to a private page (hash-verified,
SIGBUS on any failure), fork verbatim-copy with ref bump, zap
exact-once put.  New mm/ccram_residency.c holds the paths; core
touches are additive branches only.  No markers are created yet, so
this commit cannot trigger: off-mode behaviour is bit-identical.
---
